{"files": [{"path": "CWE401_Memory_Leak__malloc_realloc_int_18.c", "content": "#include "std_testcase.h"

#include <wchar.h>


void CWE401_Memory_Leak__malloc_realloc_int_18_bad()
{
    goto sink;
sink:
    {
        int * data = (int *)malloc(100*sizeof(int));
        if (data == NULL) {exit(-1);}

        data[0] = 5;
        printIntLine(data[0]);

        {
            int *tmp = (int *)realloc(data, (130000)*sizeof(int));
            if (tmp != NULL)
            {
                data = tmp;
                data[0] = 10;
                printIntLine(data[0]);
            }
            free(data);
        }
    }
}
"}], "explanation": "The original code overwrote the only pointer to the malloc'd buffer with the result of realloc. If realloc failed (returning NULL), the original allocation was leaked. The fix stores realloc's result in a temporary pointer, only replacing data on success, and always frees the still-valid pointer. Output and behavior are unchanged."}
